{"ts":"2026-07-26T06:05:39.472Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-26T06:05:39.472Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-07-26T06:05:39.471Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Class generalization 2026-07-26: the same shape was found on a second, unrelated command. pm history <id> --json reports count:7 with history:[] while compact_history carries the seven rows; --full inverts it, emptying compact_history. Two independent commands sharing the defect means the envelope contract is missing a rule for mode-inactive collection keys rather than two commands each making a local mistake. Filed pm-cyrfjq for the cross-command rule (omit the inactive collection instead of zero-filling it, contract-driven test over every command declaring mutually exclusive modes). This item stays open as the pm activity instance and its reproduction is nominated as the negative-control fixture for that rule, so it should close against the rule rather than be patched in isolation."}]}],"before_hash":"262ed9a71151db8bf11fa925845d47539cc0f3668543f7b84cfbfbbc9813baea","after_hash":"5604ac554727af20e43f27944846fba0fdc63206c00f73eb9d5531f923b1bf1e"}
